course: dictionary
lesson: 9523
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is needed. Sting can mean a sharp part pushed into your skin by a bee, wasp, jellyfish or nettle. «A honeybee's barbed sting stays in the skin» shows you the sting is that sharp part.
explain: Look at the words around sting to choose the meaning. «Soap stings your eyes» has no bee in it, so sting means a sharp burning pain. Swap your meaning into the sentence: soap burns your eyes, and that still makes sense.
explain: Sting can also mean to hurt someone's feelings, so words can sting too. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, ask: what is happening in this sentence? Then try each meaning and keep the one that fits.
fact: Sting is a verb and a noun: you can sting someone, or have a sting.
fact: The forms are sting, stings, stung and stinging.
fact: A bee's sting is also called a stinger.
fact: «Stinging nettles» are plants that can hurt you when you touch them.
fact: After any sting, tell a grown-up straight away, especially if you feel unwell, because some people are allergic and need help fast.
exercise: «After the walk, Mia was stung by a wasp.» What does stung mean here? | Ran very fast up the hill | Lost her shoes in the grass | *Pushed a sharp part into her skin and hurt her | Sang a happy song
exercise: «Soap stings your eyes.» What does sting mean? | To float on water | *A sharp burning pain | A soft, cuddly feeling | To sing loudly
exercise: «His cruel words stung her badly.» What does sting mean? | *To hurt someone's feelings | To wash her clean | To tickle her feet | To make a noise like a bell
test: Which word is a noun in «A bee sting hurt my arm»? | bee | arm | *sting | hurt
test: What does the noun sting mean in «A jellyfish sting can burn»? | *The wound or pain made by a jellyfish | A kind of fish | The sea | A loud sound
exam: After a bee sting, why should you tell a grown-up straight away? | *Because some people are allergic and may need help fast | Because bees like to be told | Because it stops the bee | Because stings are funny
